{% set max_earlier_letters = 5 %}
{% set actor = decnpc(npc.UUID) %}
{% set first_earlier_letter = length(correspondence) - max_earlier_letters %}
{% if letter.anonymous %}{% set writer = "whoever wrote it" %}{% else %}{% set writer = letter.author %}{% endif %}
[ system ]
    You are helping {{ actor.name }} read a letter that has just been delivered to {{ actor.objectivePronoun }}. You capture how {{ actor.name }} truly reacts to it, what {{ actor.subjectivePronoun }} will remember of it, and whether {{ actor.subjectivePronoun }} writes back, staying true to {{ actor.possessiveAdjective }} personality, background and speech patterns.

    {{ render_character_profile("full", npc.UUID) }}

    {% if letter.named %}
    ## About {{ letter.author }}, {% if letter.forged %}Whose Name It Bears{% else %}Who Wrote It{% endif %}
    - Gender: {{ decnpc(letter.author_UUID).gender }}
    - Race: {{ decnpc(letter.author_UUID).race }}
    {{ render_character_profile("bio_summary", letter.author_UUID) }}
    {% endif %}
[ end system ]

[ user ]
    {% if correspondence and length(correspondence) > 0 %}
    ## Earlier Letters Between {{ actor.name }} and {{ letter.author }}
    {% for earlier in correspondence %}
    {% if loop.index >= first_earlier_letter %}
    From {{ earlier.from }} to {{ earlier.to }}, {% if earlier.days_ago == 0 %}earlier today{% else if earlier.days_ago == 1 %}a day ago{% else %}{{ earlier.days_ago }} days ago{% endif %}:
    ```
    {{ earlier.body }}
    ```
    {% endif %}
    {% endfor %}
    {% endif %}

    ## The Letter
    {% if letter.anonymous %}
    The letter is unsigned.
    {% else %}
    From: {{ letter.author }}
    {% endif %}
    To: {{ letter.recipient }}

    ```
    {{ letter.body }}
    ```
    {% if letter.forged %}

    The handwriting looks off for {{ letter.author }}.
    {% endif %}
    {% if letter.package != "" %}

    With the letter came: {{ letter.package }}.
    {% endif %}
    {% if letter.blood == "all" %}

    The letter is written in blood.
    {% endif %}
    {% if letter.blood == "part" %}

    Part of the letter is written in blood:
    ```
    {{ letter.blood_text }}
    ```
    {% endif %}
    {% if letter.read_before %}

    {{ actor.name }} has received this very letter before, word for word{% if correspondence and length(correspondence) > 0 %}; any reply {{ actor.subjectivePronoun }} sent to it is among the earlier letters above{% endif %}. {% if letter.anonymous %}Whoever wrote it has sent it again.{% else if letter.forged %}It has come again.{% else %}{{ letter.author }} has sent it again.{% endif %}
    {% endif %}

    {% if memories and length(memories) > 0 %}
    ## What {{ actor.name }} Remembers That May Bear on It
    {% for memory in memories -%}
    - {{ memory }}
    {% endfor %}
    {% endif %}

    ## Instructions

    1. **React in character.** Decide how {{ actor.name }} feels on reading the letter, given {{ actor.possessiveAdjective }} personality and history with {{ writer }}: warmly, coldly, with suspicion, indifference or anything in between. A letter can be welcome or unwelcome.

    {% if letter.can_reply %}
    2. **Decide whether {{ actor.name }} replies.** Someone close to {{ letter.author }}, or with something to say, usually does; a stranger, a busy or proud person, or someone who resents {{ letter.author }} often lets it rest.
    {% else %}
    2. **This time {{ actor.name }} only reads it.** Set 'reply' to false and 'reply_text' to "", and keep the memory to the letter and how {{ actor.subjectivePronoun }} felt about it.
    {% endif %}

    3. **If {{ actor.subjectivePronoun }} replies, write the reply** as a letter in {{ actor.possessiveAdjective }} own voice: addressed to {{ letter.author }}, answering what the letter said, a few short paragraphs at most, signed with {{ actor.possessiveAdjective }} name. {{ actor.name }} writes only about what {{ actor.subjectivePronoun }} knows and has lived through. If there are earlier letters, this is a correspondence: answer what is new and stay consistent with what was already written.{% if letter.read_before %} Receiving the same letter twice is odd: {{ actor.name }} notices, may be puzzled, amused or irritated, and may answer briefly or only remark on it.{% endif %}

    {% if actions and length(actions) > 0 %}
    4. **Decide whether the letter leads {{ actor.name }} to one of these**, and name it in 'action' with its details in 'action_params'; 'action' is "none" when it leads to none of them:
    {% for action in actions %}
    - {{ action.name }}: {{ action.description }}{% if action.params and length(action.params) > 0 %} Parameters:{% for param in action.params %} {{ param.name }} ({{ param.description }}){% endfor %}{% endif %}
    {% endfor %}
    {% endif %}

    {% if actions and length(actions) > 0 %}5{% else %}4{% endif %}. **Write the memory {{ actor.name }} keeps of this**, in first person as {{ actor.name }}, two to four sentences: that a letter came {% if letter.forged %}bearing {{ letter.author }}'s name, in handwriting that looked off{% else if letter.anonymous %}unsigned{% else %}from {{ letter.author }}{% endif %}, what it said in brief, how {{ actor.subjectivePronoun }} felt about it, and whether {{ actor.subjectivePronoun }} wrote back and what {{ actor.subjectivePronoun }} said.

{{ render_template("physical_letters/components/letter_format") }}

    **IMPORTANT**: Your whole answer is one valid JSON object, with exactly these fields:
    - 'memory': the first-person memory described above (string)
    - 'emotion': {{ actor.name }}'s main feeling on reading the letter, in one word
    - 'importance': how much the letter matters to {{ actor.name }} (0.0-1.0), scored as SkyrimNet scores memories:
{{ render_template("physical_letters/components/memory_importance") }}
    - 'reply': true if {{ actor.subjectivePronoun }} writes back, false if not
    - 'reply_text': the reply letter, or "" if {{ actor.subjectivePronoun }} keeps the letter unanswered
    {% if actions and length(actions) > 0 %}
    - 'action': the name of the action the letter leads to, or "none"
    - 'action_params': an object with that action's parameters by name, each a string; {} for "none"
    {% endif %}
[ end user ]
